{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwbo4CoSx4iSCHYFufRZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its status was `ok` on its first check.\n\n**1. What the data holds:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` has about 14,000 web requests, with `timestamp` as the time field. The timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, so some are in the future. Each request records:\n- the response code (`response`)\n- the bytes sent, the host, the requested URL and the file extension\n- the client IP, the source and destination country (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`) and the OS\n- the user agent and the referer\n\nOnly three response codes appear: 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801) and 503 (441).\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-e1c3fd36 Web logs overview\"** ([open](http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-e1c3fd36-web-logs-overview-73f7306eb392)) has 7 panels:\n- Three single numbers: total requests, unique visitors (by client IP) and total bytes served.\n- Requests over time, split by response code.\n- A pie chart of each response code's share.\n- A table of the top hosts, with request count and bytes.\n- The top source countries.\n\nThe dashboard's default time range is from 7 days ago to 60 days ahead, so the future-dated part of the data shows up. I only confirmed that the panels were saved; I didn't open the dashboard to check that they draw correctly.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-e1c3fd36 5xx spike\"** (id `1b190e1c-9630-45ac-96af-745f8bc17559`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 requests with a code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. I ran the same filter directly against the index and it matched all 441 of the 503 requests.\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, so it records alerts in Kibana but sends no notifications. Adding a connector, such as Slack or email, would fix that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":22168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"output_tokens":679,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"5bfb4b9f-63f9-4c29-b8f5-101d31d29ea8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:03:52.204Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwbo3oFc3fiWTxLWhbvN"}
